{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And behold, twins.</b> Defective in yod, for all twins resemble each other, but here one was a hairy man and one was a smooth man. Esav was born circumcised and Yaakov was born circumcised. One was ruddy and one was beautiful. Esav is a pig and Yaakov is a sheep. If so, why were they born twins? Because there is no straw without grain and no grain without straw, as it is written, ״ובית עשו לקש״, and it is written, ״קדש ישראל לה׳ ראשית תבואתו״, and concerning Yaakov alone it says <b>והנה תאומים בבטנה</b>."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The text says both Esav and Yaakov were born מהול (circumcised); translated as written despite the expectation that only Yaakov would be."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:52.653761277Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}